{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2c09b7164860a6b6","name":"card_unit_182_landwehr","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_182_landwehr","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"182. LANDWEHR","text":"Becomes Veteran after you have operated units three times.","flavorText":"The Landwehr Infantry Regiment 182 was part of the 14th Landwehr Division, raised in Wehrkreis V military district during Germany’s general mobilization in 1939. The regiment came from Müllheim and served beside Landwehr Infantry Regiments 40 and 59, with Landwehr Infantry Regiment 33 joining later. These Landwehr formations drew heavily on older reservists, although the army later tried to replace older soldiers with younger men. The division first held defensive positions on the Upper Rhine under 7th Army. On 1 January 1940, it was redesignated as the 205th Infantry Division. Its former Landwehr regiments became Infantry Regiments 335, 353, and 358. After occupation duty in France and a period of demobilization, the division was recalled and sent east in 1942. On the Eastern Front, the 205th Infantry Division fought around Velizh and Velikiye Luki. Heavy losses forced reductions in 1943, but the division was later rebuilt with three grenadier regiments. During the Soviet summer offensives of 1944, it was pushed back with Army Group North through Polotsk, Daugavpils, and Livonia. It ended the war trapped in the Courland Pocket.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_182_landwehr","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_182_landwehr_title","SourceString":"182. LANDWEHR","LocalizedString":"182. LANDWEHR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_182_landwehr_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran after you have operated units three times.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran after you have operated units three times."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_182_landwehr_history","SourceString":"The Landwehr Infantry Regiment 182 was part of the 14th Landwehr Division, raised in Wehrkreis V military district during Germany’s general mobilization in 1939. The regiment came from Müllheim and served beside Landwehr Infantry Regiments 40 and 59, with Landwehr Infantry Regiment 33 joining later. These Landwehr formations drew heavily on older reservists, although the army later tried to replace older soldiers with younger men. The division first held defensive positions on the Upper Rhine under 7th Army. On 1 January 1940, it was redesignated as the 205th Infantry Division. Its former Landwehr regiments became Infantry Regiments 335, 353, and 358. After occupation duty in France and a period of demobilization, the division was recalled and sent east in 1942. On the Eastern Front, the 205th Infantry Division fought around Velizh and Velikiye Luki. Heavy losses forced reductions in 1943, but the division was later rebuilt with three grenadier regiments. During the Soviet summer offensives of 1944, it was pushed back with Army Group North through Polotsk, Daugavpils, and Livonia. It ended the war trapped in the Courland Pocket.","LocalizedString":"The Landwehr Infantry Regiment 182 was part of the 14th Landwehr Division, raised in Wehrkreis V military district during Germany’s general mobilization in 1939. The regiment came from Müllheim and served beside Landwehr Infantry Regiments 40 and 59, with Landwehr Infantry Regiment 33 joining later. These Landwehr formations drew heavily on older reservists, although the army later tried to replace older soldiers with younger men. The division first held defensive positions on the Upper Rhine under 7th Army. On 1 January 1940, it was redesignated as the 205th Infantry Division. Its former Landwehr regiments became Infantry Regiments 335, 353, and 358. After occupation duty in France and a period of demobilization, the division was recalled and sent east in 1942. On the Eastern Front, the 205th Infantry Division fought around Velizh and Velikiye Luki. Heavy losses forced reductions in 1943, but the division was later rebuilt with three grenadier regiments. During the Soviet summer offensives of 1944, it was pushed back with Army Group North through Polotsk, Daugavpils, and Livonia. It ended the war trapped in the Courland Pocket."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardOperationKreditSpent"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_182_landwehr_vet","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/182__LANDWEHR.182__LANDWEHR","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_182_landwehr_photo","SourceString":"German infantry during the Battle of Velikiye Luki, Eastern Front, 1942.","LocalizedString":"German infantry during the Battle of Velikiye Luki, Eastern Front, 1942."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryL.47"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"opCost","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_182_landwehr","owner":"card_unit_182_landwehr_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_IsLocatedOnBoard_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"Ca